<title>USA: Key staff changes expected at US FCC - sources.</title>
<headline>Key staff changes expected at US FCC - sources.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Communications Commission is expected to announce soon that the head of its international bureau is leaving and will be replaced by the chief of the agency's common carrier bureau, FCC officials said Monday.</p>
<p>Peter Cowhey, the head of the international bureau, plans to leave the agency on September 12 to spend more time with his family, officials said. He will be replaced by Regina Keeney, now the head of the common carrier bureau. It is not yet known who will replace Keeney at the powerful bureau, which oversees the local and long-distance phone industries.</p>
</text>
